35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"History teaches us that broad tools requiring universal daily input often fail, while specialized, narrow tools tend to survive and provide lasting value.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found out the capital budget is frozen... but there is some room in the software allowance. Also, per-head licenses might get very expensive as we scale.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,Oh no! I found out that the network at customer plants is super spotty and the developers are way too busy! This is a big problem!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings confirm a systemic waste of time. We are losing hours daily to redundant copying, and misrouted deliveries are happening because of inconsistent data.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It is as I feared. The coordination group is understaffed, and clerks are wasting time answering the same vendor queries repeatedly because data isn't shared.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Ryuji and @Asuka, it seems your findings align. We have a clear problem with fragmented data and redundant manual effort.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,If we choose something that requires many licenses... it might be too expensive since the capital budget is frozen.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, that's true! And if we need a fancy app for the field, the bad signal might make it crash! That would be a disaster!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"The evidence points toward a need for data consolidation. The ""everyday losses"" are caused by a lack of a single source of truth.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. However, we cannot choose a solution that adds more manual reporting to the already overburdened coordination staff.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We must be careful not to create another ""universal"" tool that everyone is forced to use daily, as those are the ones that typically vanish.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,Maybe... something with a fixed fee would be safer than per-head pricing?,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,I wonder if there's a way to fix the data without needing the developers who are busy with the accounting stuff!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,A central repository for supplier data would directly address the misrouted deliveries and the redundant vendor queries Asuka mentioned.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,A Supplier Data Hub would reduce the burden on the clerks and the coordination group by eliminating the need to hunt for the same information.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,It seems we are converging on a solution that is specific enough to be useful but broad enough to solve the data fragmentation.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think I agree. As long as it fits the software allowance.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm on board! Let's see the candidates and pick the one that doesn't need a perfect signal or a million developers!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,Agreed. The priority is reducing the measurable waste of time and errors in delivery.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,As long as it automates the retrieval of data rather than adding new manual entry tasks for the staff.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
